{
  "about": "Where a task stands, one case each: the task's status and lead, its jobs and its pull request's delivery state, as the mock reads a task detail (web/hub/mock/lifecycle.mjs), with the phase and who it waits on that crates/hive-tasks/src/lifecycle.rs derives. crates/hive-hub/src/phases.rs writes each case into a store (with `defaults` for what a case leaves out) and reads it back through the routes; what they serialize, in full, is in lifecycle-answers.json. web/hub/mock/lifecycle.test.mjs holds the mock to those answers and the Sessions list's owner rule (web/hub/src/components/chat/task-groups.ts) to the cases that wait on the owner, so none of the three can drift.",
